<title>UK: British election diary - April 23.</title>
<headline>British election diary - April 23.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a list of events in the British election campaign on Wednesday -</p>
<p>Morning - Prime Minister John Major will give press conference in Scotland on defence of union of Britain.</p>
<p>0945 GMT - Labour press conference. Details later. Leader tony Blair visits constituency outside London.</p>
<p>1000 GMT - Social Security minister Peter Lilley, Health Secretary Stephen Dorrell and Conservative party chairman Brian Mawhinney give press conference.</p>
</text>
